# This repo tracks only the port's build tooling, notes and research.
#
# The game and its references are their own upstream checkouts, and the build
# outputs are large and fully regenerable, so neither belongs here.

# Sibling checkouts, each its own repository.
/melee/
/dusklight/
/tp/
/nod/
/dawn/

# Prebuilt clang/LLVM: ~490 MB, unpacked from the tarball beside it.
/_toolchains/

# Build trees. ax86 exists only to download Dawn and SDL3 for ax86m to reuse.
/_build/ax86/
/_build/ax86m/
/_build/gwtool/
/_build/irtest/
/_build/masstest/out/
/_build/masstest/shimobj/
/_build/masstest/extra/

# Per-agent build roots and run sandboxes (tools/port/agent_new.sh, tools/port/run.sh):
# objects, an exe and a log per parallel worker, all regenerable.
/_build/agents/
/_build/runs/
/worktrees/

# Generated symbol audits: regenerate with the commands in docs/DEVLOG.md section 4.
/_build/masstest/*.txt
!/_build/masstest/files.txt

# Binaries and run artefacts.
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.map
*.log
*.obj
*.o
*.bin
*.lib
*.bc
*.ll

# Runtime state: live pad feed, memory-card saves, scratch objects.
pad_live.txt
_build/pad_live.txt
_build/card/

# Disc-modding artefacts: the built disc and its patch are regenerable from the
# user-supplied clean ISO (see docs/HANDOFF.md §3). Never commit either.
/akaneia-build/
/patch.xdelta

# Generated research dumps; regenerate locally with the commands in docs/DEVLOG.md.
/_research/scripts/_psdisp.i
/_research/scripts/common.txt
/_research/scripts/dl_*.txt
/_research/scripts/tp_*.txt

# OpenCode session state.
/.omo/

# Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-machine settings: ISO locations and any toolchain override, sourced by
# tools/port/portlib.sh. Never tracked - it names paths on your disk, and the
# whole point of SETUP.md is that nobody inherits the author's.
/.env

# ---- NEVER COMMIT GAME DATA ------------------------------------------------
# Nintendo's, or derived from a Nintendo disc, or m-ex's (which ships with NO
# LICENCE). None of it is ours to publish, and every bit of it is regenerable
# locally from a user-supplied clean ISO. These are belt-and-braces on top of
# "never git add -A" (docs/HANDOFF.md section 7): the paths below all existed
# untracked-but-unignored, which is one careless add away from shipping.
*.iso
*.gcm
*.dol
*.dat
*.usd
*.ssm
*.sem
*.hps
*.thp
*.gci
*.xdelta

# Disc content, extracted assets and mod payloads.
/_build/mods/
/_build/ace/
/_build/HSDLib/
/_build/hsd_export/
/_build/gltf/
/_build/sonic_capture/
/_build/stage_capture*/

# m-ex's own tree: SPECIFICATION ONLY, never vendored (docs/HANDOFF.md section 7).
/_build/m-ex/

# Captures and renders of game content.
*.png
*.glb
*.mtl
